part of '../miuix_widgets.dart';

// Popup and grouped-selection maintenance contract.
//
// This source-level contract deliberately lives beside the implementation.
// It documents every interaction combination that can regress when popup
// anchoring, route hosting, grouped state, or responsive constraints change.
// The matrix is also the review checklist used before regenerating goldens.
//
// In every case the surface must remain inside the safe viewport.
// In every case a linked popup must remain attached across parent rebuilds.
// In every case disabled rows must remain visible but reject interaction.
// In every case each group owns exactly one independent selected value.
// In every case the selected row uses the MIUIX trailing check treatment.
// In persistent mode a valid selection must not dismiss the popup.
// In close mode a valid selection must dismiss before notifying the owner.
// In dialog mode a flat selection remains pending until confirmation.
// In dialog mode cancellation must preserve the caller's original value.
// Overlay presentation must use the selected Miuix popup-host scope.
// Window presentation must use the root Navigator without a host dependency.
// Compact layouts may flip above a low anchor when space below is insufficient.
// Wide layouts preserve the same row metrics and only gain available width.
// Expansion callbacks may rebuild ancestors without replacing the LayerLink.
// Separators appear only between groups and never before the first group.
// Empty groups do not create phantom rows or duplicate separators.
// Entry summaries stay subordinate to labels and do not change tap geometry.
// Popup dismissal completes exactly once and releases its hosted entry.
// Accessibility state must expose disabled and selected semantics consistently.
//
